mkinitcpio-archiso
# Helper binaries for the archiso_pxe_* hooks. mkinitcpio-archiso enables those hooks by default
# (the built initramfs carries HOOKS="udev memdisk archiso archiso_loop_mnt archiso_pxe_common
# archiso_pxe_nbd archiso_pxe_http archiso_pxe_nfs"), but the binaries they pull in live in separate
# packages that were never listed here. Every build therefore ended pacstrap with three hard errors:
#     ==> ERROR: file not found: '/usr/lib/initcpio/ipconfig'      (mkinitcpio-nfs-utils)
#     ==> ERROR: binary not found: 'nbd-client'                    (nbd)
#     ==> ERROR: file not found: '/usr/lib/initcpio/nfsmount'      (mkinitcpio-nfs-utils)
#     error: command failed to execute correctly
# USB/DVD/VM boot was unaffected (that path uses archiso + archiso_loop_mnt, both intact), so this
# only ever broke PXE netboot -- but it also made every build log look like a failed build.
# Upstream archiso's own releng profile ships both packages for precisely this reason.
mkinitcpio-nfs-utils
nbd
plasma-desktop
kwin-x11
plasma-nm
plasma-pa
powerdevil
kscreen
breeze
dolphin
konsole
plymouth
brave-origin-bin
fastfetch
nvidia-settings
# nvidia-open-dkms declares "replaces/provides: nvidia-dkms", so listing
# nvidia-dkms here made pacman silently resolve to this package anyway -- the
# built ISO has always shipped nvidia-open-dkms. Naming it explicitly removes
# that provider-resolution ambiguity so the manifest matches the artifact.
# (Note: the open modules require Turing or newer; pre-Turing GPUs would need
# the proprietary nvidia-dkms instead.)
nvidia-open-dkms
linux-zen-headers

